{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Q3mBHPRmdwy3exGLQU4Xx","type":"tool_result","content":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-810-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:811:You do. The phrase is Chapter 3's, and Chapter 10 §3 named it as a pattern: **an object without its component does nothing** *[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 §3 — the object is not the implementation]*.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-812-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1122-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:1123:**An object without its component does nothing** *[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 §3 — the object is not the implementation]*. A StorageClass naming a CSI driver nobody deployed is not an exotic failure you have to imagine. It is the documented prerequisite, unmet. The claim sits unbound. The Pod sits `Pending`. `kubectl get storageclass` shows the class, healthy and correct, describing a capability that does not exist.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1124-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1472-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:1473:A) The absent-component pattern — \"an object without its component does nothing\"; the claim remains unbound\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1474-B) The eventual-consistency pattern; the claim binds after a reconciliation delay\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1629-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:1630:You now hold all four pluggable interfaces, and with them a rule you can state without help: an object without its component does nothing. You have watched that rule fire at the Ingress controller, at the network plugin, at the provisioner, and at the CSI driver — four sightings, one light. Chapter 17 will collect all four interfaces in one place and ask you what they have in common; you already know.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1631-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-600-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:601:[Omitted long matching line]\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-602-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-1323-| **Addons** | Extend the cluster rather than constituting it. DNS, Dashboard, resource monitoring, cluster-level logging. |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md:1324:| **Absent-component pattern** | An object without its component does nothing. The description exists; nothing acts on it. |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md-1325-| **The hub** | State moves through the API server, and the API server is what reads and writes etcd. Coordination is watching, not telling. (Outbound API-server→kubelet paths exist for logs, attach, and port-forward; they carry sessions, not instructions.) |\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-285-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:286:6. **An object without its component does nothing.** You have met it at least twice: a `type: LoadBalancer` Service on a cluster with no load balancer to provision, and a Service whose selector matched no Pods.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-287-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-340-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:341:*You'll also acquire one rule that outlives this chapter: an object without its component does nothing. You'll use it in Chapter 13, in Chapter 17, and on things this book never gets to.*\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-342-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-627-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:628:**An object without its component does nothing.**\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-629-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-640-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:641:> ⚓ **Worth Securing:** Chapter 3's phrase, verbatim, and worth writing on something you will see again: **an object without its component does nothing.** You have now personally met three instances: the LoadBalancer with no provider, the Service with no matching Pods, and this. Three sightings of the same light, and you stop calling it a coincidence and start calling it a landmark.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-642-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-729-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:730:**5. `[retrieval: ch3]` An object without its component does nothing.** The two Chapter 9 instances: a `type: LoadBalancer` Service on a cluster with no load balancer to provision one, and a Service whose selector matches no Pods.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-731-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1353->\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1354:> Chapter 3 gave you the sentence — *an object without its component does nothing* — and told you that you would meet it four more times. This is where that debt comes due in full.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1355->\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1393-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1394:           An object without its component does nothing.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1395-```\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1573-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1574:A) *An object without its component does nothing.* Instances: a `type: LoadBalancer` Service with no provider to fulfill it (Ch 9 §3); a Service whose selector matches no Pods (Ch 9 §4); an Ingress with no Ingress controller (Ch 10 §3); a NetworkPolicy on a plugin that does not implement NetworkPolicy (Ch 10 §7).\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1575:B) *An object without its component does nothing.* Instances: an Ingress with no Ingress controller, and a NetworkPolicy on a plugin that does not implement NetworkPolicy.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1576-C) *An object takes effect once the API server has admitted it.* Instances: the four above.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1577:D) *An object without its component does nothing.* Instances: a `type: LoadBalancer` Service with no provider; an Ingress with no controller; a NetworkPolicy on an unsupporting plugin; an Ingress whose `pathType` does not match the request path.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1578-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1801-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1802:*An object without its component does nothing.* Four instances so far:\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1803-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1855-| **Out of scope** | No TLS, no Service-name targeting, no logging, no explicit deny, no loopback blocking, and five more. |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md:1856:| **The rule** | An object without its component does nothing. Four instances of the pattern so far. Ask: *what is watching this, and is it installed?* |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-10-traffic-from-beyond-the-cluster.md-1857-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa5db13d-100b-4b10-b3c7-dabe0218186d","uuid":"bc430c3c-781a-41a8-ac92-369ad5c2a206","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:48:40.710Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-810-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:811:You do. The phrase is Chapter 3's, and Chapter 10 §3 named it as a pattern: **an object without its component does nothing** *[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 §3 — the object is not the implementation]*.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-812-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1122-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:1123:**An object without its component does nothing** *[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 §3 — the object is not the implementation]*. A StorageClass naming a CSI driver nobody deployed is not an exotic failure you have to imagine. It is the documented prerequisite, unmet. The claim sits unbound. The Pod sits `Pending`. `kubectl get storageclass` shows the class, healthy and correct, describing a capability that does not exist.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1124-\n--\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1472-\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md:1473:A) The absent-component pattern — \"an object without its component does nothing\"; the claim remains unbound\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-11-below-the-waterline.md-1474-B)