{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0192eQ2a2BD4r8zYx9GUiPi9","type":"tool_result","content":"68-#--                       different mechanisms wearing the same word\"\n69:#--   chapter-06:1036 -> \"see Ch 14 - why Helm charts have a `crds/` directory\"\n70-#-- (Four pointers, three distinct promises; 01:274 is a range pointer.)\n--\n251-\n252:IMAGE-SPECS REGEN NEEDED for ch14-fig02: two text changes inside the diagram — \"grey\" → \"gray\" (four instances; the British spelling was the structural lint's only WARN cluster) and the `crds/` annotation narrowed from \"Installed before the templates render\" to \"Installed by default on install\", which the corpus supports and the stronger claim does not.\n253--->\n--\n506-  │\n507:  ├── crds/ ──────────────► DEFINITIONS THAT MUST EXIST FIRST.\n508-  │                         Not templated. Installed by default on\n--\n569-\n570:### `crds/` — Custom Resource Definitions\n571-\n--\n782-\n783:A) `crds/`\n784-B) `templates/NOTES.txt`\n--\n809-\n810:[Omitted long matching line]\n811-\n--\n980-\n981:### Why charts have a `crds/` directory\n982-\n--\n990-\n991:So Helm carved out a directory. **`crds/` is a special directory you can create in your chart to hold your CRDs; these CRDs are not templated, but will be installed by default when running a `helm install` for the chart** [source: helm-crd-best-practices-2026-08-31]. Not templated, so there is nothing to render and nothing to sequence within. Installed by default, so getting them in is the tool's responsibility rather than the README's.\n992-\n--\n1002->\n1003:[Omitted long matching line]\n1004->\n--\n1015-| **Environment variation** | `values.yaml` — a declared surface of what may change | Overlays — declared deltas against an unmodified base |\n1016:| **Apply ordering** | `crds/` for the one case that is fatal | — (`apply -k` is still an apply; same eventual consistency, same CRD problem) |\n1017-| **Versioning** | Chart version, required on every chart; `helm list` answers what is installed | — (a directory still has no version; Git supplies one, which is Ch 15's subject) |\n--\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 40]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa5db13d-100b-4b10-b3c7-dabe0218186d","uuid":"c4497244-1630-42aa-8f6e-d82279dd866f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:49:26.339Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"68-#--                       different mechanisms wearing the same word\"\n69:#--   chapter-06:1036 -> \"see Ch 14 - why Helm charts have a `crds/` directory\"\n70-#-- (Four pointers, three distinct promises; 01:274 is a range pointer.)\n--\n251-\n252:IMAGE-SPECS REGEN NEEDED for ch14-fig02: two text changes inside the diagram — \"grey\" → \"gray\" (four instances; the British spelling was the structural lint's only WARN cluster) and the `crds/` annotation narrowed from \"Installed before the templates render\" to \"Installed by default on install\", which the corpus supports and the stronger claim does not.\n253--->\n--\n506-  │\n507:  ├── crds/ ──────────────► DEFINITIONS THAT MUST EXIST FIRST.\n508-  │                         Not templated. Installed by default on\n--\n569-\n570:### `crds/` — Custom Resource Definitions\n571-\n--\n782-\n783:A) `crds/`\n784-B) `templates/NOTES.txt`\n--\n809-\n810:[Omitted long matching line]\n811-\n--\n980-\n981:### Why charts have a `crds/` directory\n982-\n--\n990-\n991:So Helm carved out a directory. **`crds/` is a special directory you can create in your chart to hold your CRDs; these CRDs are not templated, but will be installed by default when running a `helm install` for the chart** [source: helm-crd-best-practices-2026-08-31]. Not templated, so there is nothing to render and nothing to sequence within. Installed by default, so getting them in is the tool's responsibility rather than the README's.\n992-\n--\n1002->\n1003:[Omitted long matching line]\n1004->\n--\n1015-| **Environment variation** | `values.yaml` — a declared surface of what may change | Overlays — declared deltas against an unmodified base |\n1016:| **Apply ordering** | `crds/` for the one case that is fatal | — (`apply -k` is still an apply; same eventual consistency, same CRD problem) |\n1017-| **Versioning** | Chart version, required on every chart; `helm list` answers what is installed | — (a directory still has no version; Git supplies one, which is Ch 15's subject) |\n--","numLines":40,"totalLines":67,"appliedLimit":40}}
