{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SZfoSdCrD6neDi23hL6bwS","type":"tool_result","content":"1193\t> ⚓ **Worth Securing:** *\"If you make any changes to the cluster using `kubectl edit/patch/delete`, they will be promptly reverted\"* [source: flux-concepts-2026-08-31]. Read that as principle 4 with the abstraction removed. Continuous reconciliation is not a scheduling detail. It means your manual change has a shelf life measured in minutes. This is the same property that makes a ReplicaSet recreate a Pod you deleted, and note that Argo CD, out of the box, does *not* do this [source: argocd-auto-sync-policy-2026-08-31]. Two graduated projects, four shared principles, opposite defaults.\n1194\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa5db13d-100b-4b10-b3c7-dabe0218186d","uuid":"f1e350c8-6c10-4cd3-a023-28b10919fe0f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T14:50:20.050Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/chapter-15-the-chart-is-the-truth.md","content":"> ⚓ **Worth Securing:** *\"If you make any changes to the cluster using `kubectl edit/patch/delete`, they will be promptly reverted\"* [source: flux-concepts-2026-08-31]. Read that as principle 4 with the abstraction removed. Continuous reconciliation is not a scheduling detail. It means your manual change has a shelf life measured in minutes. This is the same property that makes a ReplicaSet recreate a Pod you deleted, and note that Argo CD, out of the box, does *not* do this [source: argocd-auto-sync-policy-2026-08-31]. Two graduated projects, four shared principles, opposite defaults.\n","numLines":2,"startLine":1193,"totalLines":1651}}}
